WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.360 --> 00:00:11.510
PERTER GRINSPOON: It's very hard to know what to do as a doctor--

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:13.760
I'd say particularly as a primary care doctor--

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.580
when people come in asking for pain medications.

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:20.480
On the one hand, you don't want to not treat someone who's genuinely in pain.

00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:22.700
And the other hand, you don't want to give someone

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:25.610
pain medications who's not in pain because then you

00:00:25.610 --> 00:00:28.550
add to the black market of opioids.

00:00:28.550 --> 00:00:31.160
And the person could take it or sell it.

00:00:31.160 --> 00:00:33.380
And someone could overdose on the medication.

00:00:33.380 --> 00:00:36.500
So it's a very difficult situation whenever

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.760
someone comes in asking for opiates.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.930
I tend to be an awful person to ask for opiates just because I've

00:00:44.930 --> 00:00:46.910
suffered from opioid addiction.

00:00:46.910 --> 00:00:51.740
And a saying in recovery, which is an age

00:00:51.740 --> 00:00:55.880
old saying which is really important, is that you can't bullshit a bullshitter.

00:00:55.880 --> 00:01:00.530
And given that I've employed almost all of the tactics

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:06.110
that drug-seeking patients employ to try to get drugs out of their doctor,

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:13.270
I feel like I have a very good radar for picking up and perceiving when patients

00:01:13.270 --> 00:01:16.240
are trying to scam me for opiates.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.630
So I feel like I do a good job of that.

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:24.610
But that said, there are a lot of times in the office when it's just

00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:29.890
in the gray zone, when I just can't tell whether the patient's in pain

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.050
or whether they're trying to scam me.

00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:37.690
And then I'm faced with this really unsavory choice--

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:40.782
do I want to go home at night and feel like I was scammed.

00:01:40.782 --> 00:01:42.490
Or do I want to go home at night and feel

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:45.590
like I was this cruel doctor that didn't treat someone's pain.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.920
So you just have to decide if you want to err

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.190
on the side of giving too many medications

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:53.950
or err on the side of not giving enough medications.

00:01:53.950 --> 00:01:56.950
You know, it's interesting, I once so much

00:01:56.950 --> 00:02:01.060
didn't want to face this dilemma that I prescribed

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:05.290
Percocet for a patient that was claiming he had back pain and a limp.

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:08.257
But I went to the trouble to follow him out of the office.

00:02:08.257 --> 00:02:10.090
And I followed him for like two blocks cause

00:02:10.090 --> 00:02:11.881
I was just dying to know whether he stopped

00:02:11.881 --> 00:02:14.320
limping when no one was watching him.

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:16.570
And for the first block, he limped.

00:02:16.570 --> 00:02:18.040
A block and a half away, he limped.

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.710
But by two blocks, miraculously he was cured.

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:22.412
And he completely stopped limping.

00:02:22.412 --> 00:02:23.620
And he was walking perfectly.

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.740
So I discovered that he was completely lying to me

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.300
and scamming me for opiates.

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:30.487
So you really-- it's hard to tell.

00:02:30.487 --> 00:02:32.070
And you don't exactly know what to do.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:34.840
But you want to give people the benefit of the doubt.

00:02:34.840 --> 00:02:42.390
But opiate addiction is such that it causes people to be dishonest.

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:45.600
And it affects-- people who are so desperate for the medication

00:02:45.600 --> 00:02:48.030
that they'll flat out lie to you to get it.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:51.552
So they're very convincing because they convince themselves

00:02:51.552 --> 00:02:53.010
because they think they do need it.

00:02:53.010 --> 00:02:56.190
And they do need it, in some senses, because they're addicted.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:58.780
So it's just very hard to know what to do.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:04.080
And the answer to what do we do is that we do our best which isn't very good.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.740
But all we can do is do our best.

